module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ModulesAbelian
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SupportClosedFiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.FiniteTypeOnSiteEpi

/-!
# Properties of modules on an algebraic space: finite type and quotients

Properties of Spaces, Section 66.30 declares that the intrinsic properties of modules on a
ringed topos defined in Modules on Sites — free, finite free, generated by global sections,
locally free, finite type, quasi-coherent, of finite presentation, coherent, flat, and the rest
of that list — are applied freely to `𝒪_X`-modules on the small étale ringed site of an
algebraic space `X`.  This file records the clause of that declaration which the finiteness
arguments for supports consume: for the property "finite type", stability under quotients, and
hence under passage to the image of a map out of a module of finite type and to the cokernel of
a map into one.

Finite type on the small étale site is `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite`, local generation by
finitely many sections, recorded as an epimorphism onto the module from a finite coproduct of
copies of the structure sheaf on each member of a covering.  Composing such an epimorphism with
a given one is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi` on an arbitrary ringed site,
and the statements here are that lemma at the small étale ringed site of `X`.

Because the support of a module of finite type is closed by Stacks 07TZ, the support of a
quotient of a module of finite type is closed as well.  That is the form in which the stability
is consumed by the proper-support conditions of Stacks 0CZK, which are conditions on a *closed*
subset while the sheaves appearing in part (1) of that tag — an image, a cokernel, a
quasi-coherent quotient — are quotients of the given modules of finite type rather than modules
whose support is given to be closed.

Only the finite type clause is proved here.  Nothing is claimed for the remaining properties of
that section, nor for its four other consequences: stability of every property but coherence
under pullback, stability of every property including coherence under pullback along an étale
morphism, descent of the local properties along a surjective étale morphism, and the comparison
with the Zariski site when `X` is a scheme.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi` is the finite type clause of Properties of
  Spaces, Section 66.30, for a quotient.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteTypeOnSite_image` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteTypeOnSite_cokernel_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`: the image of a
  map out of a module of finite type, and the cokernel of a map into one, are of finite type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosed_supportOfSheaf_of_epi`: the support of a quotient of a
  module of finite type is closed.

## Implementation notes

The module universe is pinned to the universe of the schemes, because
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi` is stated with the sections of the modules in
the universe of the sheaf of rings, and the small étale ringed site of an algebraic space has
its structure sheaf valued in the universe of the schemes.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiniteTypeOnSite_cokernel` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentStalkLocalProperties` is a different statement
about the same object: it asks both modules to be coherent and concludes through coherence of
the cokernel, whereas `isFiniteTypeOnSite_cokernel_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite` below asks only that
the target be of finite type.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isClosed_supportOfSheaf_of_epi` is the step carried out inline inside
the proof of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasProperSupport_of_epi` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentAdicSystemProperSupport`; it is named here so that
closedness of the support of a quotient can be used without the proper-support conclusion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07TZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07TZ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)

/-- **Properties of Spaces, Section 66.30, the finite type clause for a quotient.**  A quotient
of an `𝒪_X`-module of finite type on the small étale site of an algebraic space `X` is again of
finite type.

On each member of a covering witnessing finite type for the source, the restricted epimorphism
composes with the finite coproduct presenting the source to present the target. -/
@[stacks 05VR "finite type, quotients"]
theorem isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi {M N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite M) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite N :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi p hM

/-- The image of a map of `𝒪_X`-modules whose source is of finite type on the small étale site
is of finite type, because the canonical map onto the image is an epimorphism. -/
theorem isFiniteTypeOnSite_image {M N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite M) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite (Abelian.image f) :=
  isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X hX (Abelian.factorThruImage f) hM

/-- The cokernel of a map of `𝒪_X`-modules whose target is of finite type on the small étale
site is of finite type, because the projection onto the cokernel is an epimorphism. -/
theorem isFiniteTypeOnSite_cokernel_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite
    {M N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (hN : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite N) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite (cokernel f) :=
  isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X hX (cokernel.π f) hN

/-- The support of a quotient of an `𝒪_X`-module of finite type on the small étale site is
closed in the point set of `X`: the quotient is again of finite type, and the support of a
module of finite type is closed by Stacks 07TZ. -/
theorem isClosed_supportOfSheaf_of_epi {M N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite M) :
    IsClosed (supportOfSheaf B S hS X ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf _).obj N)) :=
  let := isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X hX p hM
  isClosed_supportOfSheaf_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite B S hS X hX N

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
